A.u0. {"problem": "The diff and the final file disagree about the `deliver` action. The diff sets the action and its `approved` precondition to `status: proposed`, but the file after the change shows both as `confirmed`. Either way the record is wrong. If the file is right, `deliver` is marked confirmed, with the source re-pointed to interview line L31 and no quote, without any quoted person confirming `staging`. If the diff is right, an element is proposed while the rest of the file is confirmed, and the file as shown does not reflect it.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, action deliver (source, status, precondition approved)", "kind": "other", "from": "llm"}
A.u1. {"problem": "The `approved` precondition and the `deliver_approved_commit` handoff still cite interview L8 ('20번, 21번 둘 다 추천대로 동의'). That confirmation covered delivery to `local` only, so it does not back the widened rule. The action's source now points at L31 with no quote, so the quote that justified the deliver rules no longer matches the rule they sit under.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, deliver.preconditions[approved].source and handoffs.deliver_approved_commit.source", "kind": "reference", "from": "llm"}
A.u2. {"problem": "Delivery has no `staging` Environment. The only Environment fixture is `ENV-local`, every DeliveryRequest fixture uses `environment: local`, and `DeliveryRequest.environment` is an unconstrained string. A staging request is accepted but nothing in delivery models or tests where it goes. No scenario covers a staging delivery or the `deliver` action in either domain.", "where": "delivery.domain.yaml, world.fixtures / Environment / scenarios; authoring.domain.yaml scenarios", "kind": "behaviour", "from": "llm"}
A.u3. {"problem": "The `deliver` params enum, which is part of the authoring interface, was widened but the version was not bumped. Authoring stays at `version: 16`, and the composition still pins `interface: 1` for both members. Consumers cannot tell that `deliver` now accepts a new value.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml version; toprope-self.composition.yaml members", "kind": "other", "from": "llm"}
A.u4. {"problem": "The glossary and purpose statements describe delivery as a single path to 'the environment' (the delivery purpose announcement: 'reach the environment'; the delivery success metric). With staging added, a staging deploy that is verified counts toward 'verified-in-use' the same as a local one, and the wording no longer says which environment is meant.", "where": "delivery.domain.yaml purpose.announcement, success_metric, glossary 'delivery request'", "kind": "reference", "from": "llm"}
A.u5. {"problem": "The diff changes the `deliver` action's source to interview L31 with no quote and sets the action and its `approved` precondition to `status: proposed`. The listed post-change file shows both as `confirmed`, so the file and the diff disagree about their status. The only confirmed evidence behind `deliver` (L8, '20번, 21번 둘 다 추천대로 동의') was given when `environment` was `local`. Nothing quoted shows the owner agreed to `staging`. Either the new value is labelled confirmed without a person's confirmation, or the precondition's confirmation was dropped and the domain now carries unconfirmed elements.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, actions.deliver (source, status, and preconditions.approved)", "kind": "contradiction", "from": "llm"}
A.u6. {"problem": "Widening the `deliver` `environment` enum changes the public action contract, but the domain `version` is still 16 and the composition still pins `interface: 1`. A consumer built against the old contract is not told that a new environment value can now flow through the handoff.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, version; toprope-self.composition.yaml, members.authoring.interface", "kind": "other", "from": "llm"}
A.u7. {"problem": "Delivery was not updated for `staging`. Its only `Environment` fixture is `ENV-local`, and every `DeliveryRequest` fixture and scenario uses `local`. `request_delivery.environment` is a free string, so a `staging` handoff is accepted. But no `staging` Environment is declared for it to point at, and nothing covers a staging delivery. Delivery's environment handling for `staging` is untested and unspecified.", "where": "delivery.domain.yaml, objects.Environment, world.fixtures, actions.request_delivery.params.environment", "kind": "reference", "from": "llm"}
A.u8. {"problem": "No authoring scenario exercises `deliver`, so neither the new `staging` value nor the existing `local` value is checked end to end through the `deliver_approved_commit` handoff. The handoff's `target` key includes `params.environment`, so a `staging` delivery of a commit already delivered to `local` is a new target, and that behaviour is untested.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, scenarios and handoffs.deliver_approved_commit", "kind": "behaviour", "from": "llm"}
A.u9. {"problem": "The change request gives no reason (\"Why:\" is empty), and the new source `interview.jsonl#L31` has no quote. The `deliver` action is a confirmed element, and the diff downgrades its precondition `approved` and the action itself to `proposed`. Yet the post-change file shows both as `confirmed`, with the action now citing an unquoted L31. Either way, staging delivery is marked confirmed without a person's quoted confirmation, and the diff and the file disagree about the status.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, actions.deliver (source, status, precondition `approved`)", "kind": "other", "from": "llm"}
A.u10. {"problem": "Authoring's `deliver` now accepts `staging`, but Delivery does not know it. `Environment` is only declared with `local` (fixture ENV-local), and every DeliveryRequest fixture and scenario uses `local`. `request_delivery.environment` is a free string, so nothing validates the value. A staging handoff would create a request for an Environment that does not exist in Delivery, and nothing in the deploy or probe flow covers it.", "where": "delivery.domain.yaml, objects.Environment / world fixtures / request_delivery.params.environment", "kind": "behaviour", "from": "llm"}
A.u11. {"problem": "The `deliver` action's enum was widened, which changes Authoring's interface, but the domain `version` is still 16. There is no scenario covering `deliver` with `staging`. The composition still pins `interface: 1`, and the handoff targets Delivery `1.x`. The compatibility of the widened handoff payload with Delivery is not checked or reflected.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml version; toprope-self.composition.yaml members/wiring; handoffs.deliver_approved_commit", "kind": "reference", "from": "llm"}
A.u12. {"problem": "The handoff and the `deliver` precondition `approved` both cite the interview lines (L8, \"20번, 21번 둘 다 추천대로 동의\") that agreed the original local-only delivery. The glossary says only commits on main are delivered and the deploy floor assumes one environment. Neither describes staging or whether staging needs different approval. Existing rules were not revisited for the new environment.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, handoffs.deliver_approved_commit source; glossary.main", "kind": "reference", "from": "llm"}
A.u13. {"problem": "The change request only widens the environment enum, but the diff also downgrades the `deliver` action and its `approved` precondition from confirmed to proposed. It swaps the action's source from interview L8 (quote '20번, 21번 둘 다 추천대로 동의.') to L31 with no quote. Nothing in the request asks for this, and no confirming evidence for L31 is cited. The `deliver_approved_commit` handoff, which is still confirmed, depends on `deliver`. The 'every file after the change' listing contradicts the diff: it shows `status: confirmed` on both and a confirmed-looking L31 source. So the diff and the file disagree about the state being deployed.", "where": "authoring/authoring.domain.yaml, action deliver (status, source, precondition `approved`) and handoff deliver_approved_commit", "kind": "other", "from": "llm"}
A.u14. {"problem": "Delivering to `staging` is now allowed, but the delivery domain has no support for it. The world has only an `ENV-local` Environment fixture, and no action ever sets `Environment.current_commit`. Every DeliveryRequest fixture and scenario uses `local`, and `DeliveryRequest.environment` is a free string. Nothing declares or exercises a `staging` environment, and nothing keeps delivery's environments in step with the authoring enum. The delivery purpose and glossary still speak of 'the environment' in the singular. The new behaviour is untested and undeclared on the receiving side.", "where": "delivery/delivery.domain.yaml, object Environment, world fixtures, scenarios, purpose and glossary; authoring deliver.params.environment", "kind": "reference", "from": "llm"}
A.u15. {"problem": "The `deliver` parameter enum gains a value, which changes authoring's interface, but the domain `version` stays at 16. The composition still pins `interface: 1` for both members. No scenario in authoring covers `deliver` or the handoff for either environment.", "where": "authoring/authoring.domain.yaml version; toprope-self.composition.yaml members; scenarios", "kind": "behaviour", "from": "llm"}
A.u16. {"problem": "The diff does more than the request asks. It sets the deliver action's `approved` precondition to status proposed, and sets the action's own source and status to proposed. It also replaces the action's source with interview line L31, which has no quote and is not about delivery to staging. The precondition's L8 quote ('20번, 21번 둘 다 추천대로 동의') and its confirmed status were the only recorded owner agreement for the 'only an approved commit is delivered' rule. The after-change file does not match the diff: it shows the action as confirmed with the L31 source, and the precondition as confirmed with the L8 quote. So what gets deployed is unclear, and either version loses or blurs provenance for a rule that was already confirmed.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, actions.deliver (precondition `approved`, action source and status)", "kind": "other", "from": "llm"}
A.u17. {"problem": "Delivery has no staging environment. The only Environment fixture is ENV-local, and every DeliveryRequest fixture and scenario uses `local`. The `environment` param is a free string in Delivery, so a `staging` request is accepted but nothing models it and nothing exercises it. No Authoring scenario covers `deliver` with `staging`, so the handoff of `params.environment` and the target key `domain:commit:environment` are untested for the new value.", "where": "delivery.domain.yaml, world.fixtures (Environment) and scenarios; authoring.domain.yaml, handoffs.deliver_approved_commit", "kind": "behaviour", "from": "llm"}
A.u18. {"problem": "Widening the `deliver` environment enum changes the Authoring interface that Delivery consumes (`interface: 1.x`). The composition pins interface 1 on both members and Delivery's declaration is unchanged, so nothing shows that Delivery or the composition was checked or versioned for the new value. Delivery's glossary and `deploy` text also assume a single `local` target.", "where": "toprope-self.composition.yaml, members and wiring; delivery.domain.yaml, request_delivery.params.environment", "kind": "reference", "from": "llm"}

