B.u0. {"problem": "The change makes `deliver` accept `staging`, but Delivery has no matching support. The world fixtures declare only `ENV-local`, with no staging Environment. Every DeliveryRequest fixture is 'all with environment local'. No worked example delivers to staging. A `staging` handoff therefore points at an Environment that the declaration does not define, and nothing exercises or tests the new path.", "where": "SKILL.md, Delivery World fixtures (Environment ENV-local, requests R1–R6); EXAMPLES.md Delivery section", "kind": "reference"}
B.u1. {"problem": "Delivery's `request_delivery` and `DeliveryRequest.environment` take any string, so the new enum value is not matched on the receiving side. Delivery's rules, preconditions and deploy floor are the same for every environment. The stated reason is a shared environment before real users, but nothing separates staging from local or makes it a gate before wider release. Nothing stops a request for any other environment name either.", "where": "SKILL.md, Delivery Objects (DeliveryRequest.environment: string), Actions (request_delivery) and 'What the receiver needs' in the Handoff section", "kind": "behaviour"}
B.u2. {"problem": "The change edits an action's parameter enum but leaves the header versions untouched ('Authoring declaration version 12', interface 1). The accepted-value set of a handoff-triggering action has changed, and the version records do not reflect that.", "where": "SKILL.md, header line (Authoring declaration version 12, interface 1)", "kind": "other"}
B.u3. {"problem": "The header still says Authoring declaration version 12, but the `deliver` action's `environment` enum was widened to include `staging`. The accepted input of a declared action has changed, so the declaration version should be bumped. As written, the SKILL does not show that the declaration changed.", "where": "SKILL.md header line ('Authoring declaration version 12'), Authoring `deliver` action", "kind": "reference"}
B.u4. {"problem": "Delivery has no `staging` counterpart. The only Environment fixture is ENV-local, and all DeliveryRequest fixtures are stated to have environment local. Delivery's `environment` param is a free string, so it never validates that `staging` is a known Environment. A staging delivery therefore points at an Environment object that does not exist in the world, and the probes and verify flow is never exercised against it.", "where": "SKILL.md Delivery 'World fixtures (Delivery)' and DeliveryRequest.environment / Environment object", "kind": "behaviour"}
B.u5. {"problem": "No worked example or scenario covers `deliver` with `environment = staging`, or the handoff to Delivery. No example for `deliver` exists at all. EXAMPLES.md Delivery scenarios use only local requests, so the new behaviour is untested.", "where": "EXAMPLES.md (Authoring and Delivery sections)", "kind": "other"}
B.u6. {"problem": "The change is meant to make staging a shared step before anything reaches real users. Nothing in the rules enforces or records that order. The `deliver` precondition checks only `approved`, and the deploy floor and `verify` do not depend on environment. A commit can therefore be delivered straight to local, or to any environment, without ever being verified in staging, so the stated purpose is not enforced.", "where": "SKILL.md Authoring Preconditions `deliver`/approved; Delivery deploy floor glossary", "kind": "behaviour"}
B.u7. {"problem": "Delivery was not updated for staging. Its Environment object has only the fixture ENV-local, and its fixtures, glossary and announcement describe a single environment. DeliveryRequest.environment is a free string, so a staging request passes in without any matching Environment. The deploy floor and the Environment object's current_commit are never tied to the requested environment, so nothing records that staging points at a deployed commit. The 'shared environment before the people who use the domain' purpose is not expressed anywhere in Delivery.", "where": "SKILL.md, Delivery: Objects (Environment), World fixtures (only ENV-local), Purpose/Announcement", "kind": "reference"}
B.u8. {"problem": "The change adds a new enum value for deliver but no scenario exercises it. There is no example of deliver with environment staging or local, or of a staging request flowing through the handoff to request_delivery. The Authoring examples never cover deliver, and the Delivery examples only use fixtures with environment local.", "where": "EXAMPLES.md, Authoring and Delivery scenarios; SKILL.md Delivery World fixtures", "kind": "other"}
B.u9. {"problem": "The deliver action's parameter enum changed, which alters the declaration, but the stated 'Authoring declaration version 12' and the interface version were not bumped. Delivery's receiving side is described as taking any string, so the handoff contract is not updated to say which environments are valid.", "where": "SKILL.md header (Authoring declaration version 12), Handoff section 'What the receiver needs'", "kind": "other"}
B.u10. {"problem": "Delivery never uses the environment, so choosing `staging` has no effect. `request_delivery` stores `environment` on the DeliveryRequest, but the kernel services `preview`, `deploy` and `probe` are called only with domain, commit and approver. Nothing passes `target.environment`. A `staging` request would therefore build, deploy and probe exactly as a `local` one, and could land in the wrong place. That defeats the stated purpose of a shared environment before real users. This worked before only because `local` was the sole option.", "where": "SKILL.md, Delivery actions preview, deploy and run_probes (kernel service calls); Handoff `deliver_approved_commit` parameters", "kind": "behaviour"}
B.u11. {"problem": "Delivery was not updated for a second environment. The only Environment fixture is ENV-local, and all fixture requests use `local`. `DeliveryRequest.environment` is a free string with no precondition checking it is a known environment. The Purpose and Announcement still say 'the environment' in the singular, and the glossary does not mention staging. Delivery cannot tell staging from local or from a typo, and there is no Environment record for staging to point at a deployed commit.", "where": "SKILL.md, Delivery: Objects (Environment), World fixtures, Purpose, request_delivery params and preconditions", "kind": "reference"}
B.u12. {"problem": "No worked example or scenario covers delivering to `staging`, either the Authoring `deliver` action with `environment = staging` or the handoff into Delivery. The existing Delivery examples all use `local`. The new path is untested, and the handoff's environment-dependent target string is never exercised with staging.", "where": "EXAMPLES.md (Authoring and Delivery); SKILL.md Handoff `deliver_approved_commit`", "kind": "other"}
B.u13. {"problem": "The Authoring `deliver` parameter changed, but the declaration version ('Authoring declaration version 12') and interface version were not bumped. The handoff is typed against `interface 1.x`. Delivery may not accept the new value, so the change silently widens the contract with the receiving domain.", "where": "SKILL.md header (Authoring declaration version 12); Handoff 'What the receiver needs'", "kind": "other"}
B.u14. {"problem": "The change adds `staging` to the `deliver` enum, but Delivery only knows one environment. The Environment object is fixtured only as ENV-local, and every DeliveryRequest fixture says 'all with environment local'. No action creates or updates an Environment, and DeliveryRequest.environment is a free string. A staging delivery therefore has no Environment to point at its deployed commit. Delivery's Purpose, Glossary and fixtures still describe a single 'the environment'. No fixture, example or scenario covers a staging delivery, so the new value is untested.", "where": "SKILL.md, Delivery: Objects (Environment), World fixtures (Delivery), Authoring: Actions (deliver); EXAMPLES.md (no staging scenario)", "kind": "reference"}
B.u15. {"problem": "The Authoring `deliver` interface now accepts a new value that crosses the handoff to Delivery's `request_delivery`, which still takes 'environment' as an unconstrained string. The header still says 'Authoring declaration version 12' and interface 1, and the handoff still targets Delivery interface `1.x`. Nothing records that the accepted values changed, and nothing makes Delivery validate or handle `staging`.", "where": "SKILL.md header (declaration versions); Handoff deliver_approved_commit; Delivery request_delivery", "kind": "other"}

