C.u0. {"problem": "Authoring can now send `environment: staging`, but Delivery declares and seeds only an `ENV-local` Environment. Every DeliveryRequest fixture and scenario uses `local`. No staging Environment exists to point at a deployed commit, and `DeliveryRequest.environment` is a free string, so Delivery never checks that the value is a known environment. A staging delivery would reach Delivery with no matching environment, and nothing in the declarations covers that case.", "where": "delivery/delivery.domain.yaml, objects.Environment and world.fixtures; authoring.deliver params.environment", "kind": "reference"}
C.u1. {"problem": "The new `staging` value is not covered by any scenario. The only Authoring scenarios exercise approve, confirm, decide and fetch, with no `deliver` scenario. The Delivery scenarios run only with `local`. The handoff's dedupe target `domain:commit:environment` and per-environment behaviour such as the 'not a downgrade' floor and verification are therefore untested for staging.", "where": "authoring scenarios and handoffs.deliver_approved_commit; delivery scenarios", "kind": "behaviour"}
C.u2. {"problem": "The `deliver` action's params gained a new allowed value, which changes what Authoring hands to Delivery. The authoring `version` stays at 13 and the composition member interface stays at 1. The `deliver` action and its precondition still cite interview L8 ('20번, 21번 둘 다 추천대로 동의'). That answer predates the staging request and was not shown to cover it.", "where": "authoring/authoring.domain.yaml, version and actions.deliver source; toprope-self.composition.yaml members", "kind": "other"}
C.u3. {"problem": "The new `staging` value is passed to Delivery as `environment`, but Delivery never uses it when it acts. The `preview`, `deploy` and `run_probes` calls send only the domain and commit (and approver for `deploy`), not the environment. A staging request would therefore run through the same steps as a local one, with nothing to say where it should land. Probing and verification would not tell the two apart either. Delivery's `deploy` still describes only the single, local target.", "where": "delivery/delivery.domain.yaml, actions preview, deploy and run_probes (call `with` lists); authoring deliver and handoff deliver_approved_commit", "kind": "behaviour"}
C.u4. {"problem": "Delivery declares an Environment object (\"Where a domain runs; it points at one deployed commit\") but only the fixture `ENV-local`. Nothing declares a `staging` Environment. `DeliveryRequest.environment` stays a free string, so Delivery does not check that `staging` exists, and a staging request has no Environment object to point at the deployed commit. No Delivery scenario or fixture exercises a staging request.", "where": "delivery/delivery.domain.yaml, object Environment, world fixtures and scenarios", "kind": "reference"}
C.u5. {"problem": "The enum on a public action param widened but `version` stays 13. The composition still pins `interface: 1`. A new accepted value changes the interface that consumers rely on, so the version is not bumped. The `deliver` action's source and quote (the interview line agreeing to items 20 and 21) are unchanged and say nothing about staging. The widening has no recorded decision behind it, even though it exposes a shared environment.", "where": "authoring/authoring.domain.yaml, `version` and action deliver (params.environment, source)", "kind": "other"}
C.u6. {"problem": "No scenario covers `deliver` with `environment: staging`, or the handoff to Delivery with that value. The handoff target `domain:commit:environment` is built from it, but nothing checks that a staging delivery stays separate from a local one or reaches Delivery's `request_delivery`.", "where": "authoring/authoring.domain.yaml, scenarios and handoffs.deliver_approved_commit", "kind": "other"}
C.u7. {"problem": "Delivery never uses the environment it receives. The `deploy`, `preview` and `run_probes` calls pass only domain, commit and approver, with no environment. A `staging` request would therefore be built, deployed and probed with no sign of targeting staging, and could deploy to the same place as `local`. Delivery has no way to deliver to staging, so the change would look like it works while doing the wrong thing.", "where": "delivery/delivery.domain.yaml, actions deploy, preview and run_probes (`call` `with` blocks); authoring.domain.yaml action deliver and the deliver_approved_commit handoff", "kind": "behaviour"}
C.u8. {"problem": "Delivery has no `staging` Environment. Only ENV-local is declared as a fixture, and `DeliveryRequest.environment` is a free string that nothing checks against Environment. A `staging` request is accepted by Delivery but matches no declared Environment, so `current_commit` is never tracked for staging. No delivery scenario or fixture covers a staging request either.", "where": "delivery/delivery.domain.yaml, object Environment, world fixtures and scenarios; authoring.domain.yaml action deliver", "kind": "reference"}
C.u9. {"problem": "The `deliver` params enum and the `deliver_approved_commit` handoff change what Authoring sends to Delivery (a new environment value), but Authoring's version stays 13 and the composition still pins interface 1 for both members. A consumer pinned to the old interface gets no signal that a new value can arrive. Delivery's own fixtures and scenarios assume `local` only.", "where": "authoring/authoring.domain.yaml version and deliver action; toprope-self.composition.yaml members", "kind": "other"}
C.u10. {"problem": "The `deliver` action and its enum cite the interview quote 'agree with recommendations for 20 and 21' (L8), which approved delivery to `local` only. The new `staging` value is still marked `status: confirmed` with that same source, though no person confirmed it. It has no scenario in Authoring either.", "where": "authoring/authoring.domain.yaml, action deliver (params.environment enum, source/status); scenarios", "kind": "other"}
C.u11. {"problem": "Staging is accepted at the handoff, but Delivery never uses the request's environment when it acts. The preview, deploy and run_probes calls pass only domain and commit (plus approver for deploy). Deployments, probes and the floor's 'not a downgrade' check have no way to target staging. A staging request would build, deploy and probe whichever environment the kernel defaults to, probably local, and could still be marked verified. This was harmless while local was the only value, but it now breaks.", "where": "delivery/delivery.domain.yaml, actions preview, deploy and run_probes (call `with` lacks environment); authoring deliver_approved_commit passes params.environment", "kind": "behaviour"}
C.u12. {"problem": "Delivery declares only one Environment, `ENV-local`, and every DeliveryRequest fixture and scenario uses local. Nothing declares a `staging` Environment, and no scenario covers delivering to it, so the new value is never exercised or checked. The Environment object ('points at one deployed commit') has no staging instance to point at.", "where": "delivery/delivery.domain.yaml, world.fixtures and scenarios; authoring deliver (no scenario)", "kind": "reference"}
C.u13. {"problem": "Authoring's interface contract changed, since `deliver` now accepts a new value. The domain `version` stays 13, and the composition and handoff still pin interface 1 / 1.x. Delivery's `environment` stays an unconstrained string and its version stays 6. The change is not versioned, so consumers and the change check cannot see that the accepted environments widened.", "where": "authoring/authoring.domain.yaml `version: 13`; toprope-self.composition.yaml members/wiring; delivery request_delivery params.environment", "kind": "other"}
